hadiths[153]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2385","Sayyiduna Shareed (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked that my mother (Sahiba) owes the expiation of freeing a neck and I have a black Abyssinian slave girl, will she be enough? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Call her and bring her.\"" When she came"
"2386","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Your oath will be based on what your Sahib (companion) considers you to be truthful.\"""""
"2387","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The oath of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, was like this: \Laa wa muqalib al-qulubbi\"""
"2388","Sayyiduna Abu Sharh al-Khuza'i (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: \Whoever is bled or injured"
"2389","It was narrated from Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Hazm on the authority of Abia on the authority of Jeddah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, wrote a decree for the people of Yemen, and in this letter it was: \Whoever kills a Muslim without reason and the witnesses prove that blood is on him"
"2390","Sahl bin Abi Hatmah said: Abdullah bin Sahl bin Abi Hatmah, a member of Banu Haritha, went to Khyber with some people of his people in search of livelihood, Abdullah was raped, he was killed, his neck was twisted and the seals (beads) were broken (i.e. his neck was badly crushed) and his body was thrown into one of the springs of Khyber, his companions shouted and took out his body. Then those people came to Madinah Tayyaba to serve the Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Sahl, may God bless him and grant him peace, the brother of the deceased, who was an old companion of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his cousins, Hawaisah and Muhaisa Ibna Masud, were with him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: \Let the elders speak\"""
"2391","It was narrated from Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm on the authority of Abiyyah on the authority of Jeddah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent a letter to the people of Yemen that said: \A man should be killed in exchange for a woman.\"""""
"2392","It was narrated on the authority of Anas that a girl's head was crushed between two stones. Even when the Jew's name was mentioned, he nodded his head in support, so he was called and he confessed, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered and his head was also crushed between two stones."
"2393","Abu Juhaifa said: I asked Sayyiduna Ali (RA): O Commander of the Faithful! Do you have anything other than the Book of Allah as a revelation? (i.e. that which is not in the Holy Qur'an), he said: No, by the One who split the grain and created the soul, I do not know anything except the Qur'an except the understanding (and insight) which Allah bestows upon whom He wills of His Book, and which is written in the leaf. I said: What is written in this leaf? He said: The commandments of the day and the release of prisoners and the issue that a Muslim should not be killed in exchange for an infidel."
"2394","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Do not set limits (punishments) inside the mosque"
"2395","On the authority of Sayyidna Samura bin Jundab, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever kills his slave"
"2396","Sayyiduna Wail bin Hajar (RA) said: I was in the service of the Prophet (PBUH) at that time. A murderer was brought to him tied with a belt. The Prophet (PBUH) said to the guardian of the deceased: \Will you forgive this murderer?\"" He said: No"
"2397","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The major sins are: associating partners with Allah"
"2398","On the authority of Sayyidna Thabit bin Dahhak, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Cursing a believer is equivalent to murder"
"2399","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: “He who commits suicide with an iron will have that weapon in his hand which he will keep barking in his stomach, and will remain forever in the Hellfire, and whoever commits suicide by eating poison, his poison will be in his hand which he will always drink in the Hellfire, and whoever kills himself by falling from a mountain will always fall into the Hellfire. Will do."
"2400","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: A man killed a man during the time of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, set his death penalty at 12,000 dirhams. They could not do it, and those disbelievers were not angry except because Allah and the Messenger made them rich out of His bounty (At-Tawbah: 74/9) i.e. by taking money."
"2401","On the authority of Sayyidna Amr bin Hazm, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote to the people of Yemen: \The duet on those who sleep is one thousand dinars.\"" (i.e. those who have gold)"""
"2402","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Amr bin Hazm that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote in the letter that he sent to the people of Yemen: \In the name of Allah"
"2403","Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Hazm narrated on the authority of his father from his grandfather (Sayyidna Amr bin Hazm, may God be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote to the people of Yemen, in which it was written: \And there is a full amount of money in the nose when you cut it from the root"
"2404","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, defined the crime of murder as five types."
"2405","It was narrated from Imran bin Hussain (RA) that the slave of the poor cut off the hand of the slave of the rich. His owner came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH). The people said: O Messenger of Allah (PBUH)! This slave belongs to the faqirs (i.e. those who cannot pay dowry), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not impose anything (duet) on them."
"2406","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Musa Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The fingers are all equal.\"" Sayyidina Abu Musa said: There are ten (on each finger). He said: \""Yes.\"""""
"2407","On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \This and these (all) are equal\"" and pointed to the finger and thumb."""
"2408","Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Hazm narrated from his grandfather on the authority of his father that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote to the people of Yemen that: \For every finger and toe there are ten camels (dayat).\"""""
"2409","Amr ibn Shuaib narrated from his grandfather on the authority of his father: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, prescribed a diet of five camels for wounds that reach the bone."
"2410","Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm narrated from his grandfather on the authority of his father that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote to the people of Yemen: \And there are ten camels in each finger and toe"
"2411","Amr ibn Shuaib narrated from his father and then from his grandfather: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided on the diet of five camels in their teeth."
"2412","Abu Bakr bin Muhammad Amr bin Hazm narrated from his grandfather on the authority of his father that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote for the people of Yemen: \And there are five camels in the tooth.\"""""
"2413","It was narrated from Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (RA) that a man bit a man's hand with a tooth, so he pulled his hand from the biter's mouth, which broke two of his front teeth. Then he brought his dispute to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH), and the Prophet (PBUH) said: \You bite your own brother with the tooth like a camel bites"
"2414","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \If a chopper injures someone"
"2415","It has been narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) in this chain of transmission as mentioned above."
"2416","It has been narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) in this chain of transmission as mentioned above."
"2417","On the authority of Sayyidna Mugheera bin Shuba, may Allah be pleased with him, he narrates from the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that two women were married to the same man, one of them had a disagreement due to the other's honor, so one of them struck the other with an iron rod, as a result of which the other woman died and her unborn child also died. He put this woman's money on the woman's aqeela."
"2418","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may God be pleased with him) narrated that Sayyidna Umar ibn al-Khattab (may God be pleased with him) sought the decision of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding the fetus, and Hamal ibn Malik ibn Nabagha stood up and said: I was in the middle of two women. He ordered the killing of the woman who had beaten her, that is, by declaring it a premeditated murder, he decided to kill the woman in revenge."
"2419","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira that two women of Hazail tribe fought and one hit the other with a stone, which killed her and what was in her stomach also perished. The heirs of the murdered woman brought this dispute to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of God be upon him, so he decided on a slave or a concubine instead of the fetus (abdomen) and placed the dowry of the murdered woman on the relatives of the murdered woman, and declared the heirs of this dowry to the children and husband of the murdered woman, etc. At that time, Hamal bin Nabagha Hazli said: O Messenger of God! How should we reward a child who neither drank, nor ate, nor spoke, nor shouted, such an order is not reliable. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \This is evident from the brothers of the priests"
"2420","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The body of a person killed by a crime or suspect"
"2421","Sayyidna Sahl bin Saad al-Saadi, may God be pleased with him, reported that a man began to look in through a hole in the door of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had an iron comb in his hand at that time, with which he, may God bless him and grant him peace, was combing his head. He said: \The order to take permission has been given so as not to be seen.\"""""
"2422","Sayyiduna Sahl bin Saad (RA) said: When the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) was combing his hair with an iron comb in the room, one of the Companions started peeking in. The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \If I had known that you were peeking"
"2423","Sayyiduna Muti' (may Allah be pleased with him) said: On the day of the conquest of Makkah, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: \After today"
"2424","It has been narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Muti, may Allah be pleased with him, and the translation is the same as mentioned above. \n Imam Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: In the commentary of the above mentioned hadith, the scholars have said that it means that all Qureshi will become Muslims and no one will die in disbelief, that is, from now on, no Qureshi will remain a disbeliever and if he commits a crime, he will be killed."
"2425","Sayyiduna Abu Musa said: I came to Madinah with my son. We did not see the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him. I went to him, he came out wearing double clothes. I said: By the Lord of the Kaaba, this is my boy. He said: \Is this your son?\"" He said: Yes"
"2426","Sayyiduna Abu Musa (RA) said: I attended the service of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) with my father, and he (PBUH) said to my father: \Is this your son?\"" He said: Yes"
"2427","(Mawquf Hadith) Muhammad ibn Kathir informed us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from 'Abdullah ibn Salam, who said: ""A group of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sat and discussed. We said: 'If we knew which deed is most beloved to Allah, we would do it.' So Allah revealed: 'Whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth exalts Allah, and He is the Exalted in Might, the Wise' (Al-Hashr 59:1) until its end."" 'Abdullah said: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) recited it to us until its end."" Abu Salamah said: ""Ibn Salam recited it to us."" Yahya said: ""Abu Salamah recited it to us, Yahya recited it to us, al-Awza'i recited it to us, and Muhammad recited it to us."""
"2428","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Whoever knowing the truth of Allah's word and going out for Jihad in the way of Allah only with the intention of Jihad"
"2429","Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah (PBUH)! Which is the best Jihad? He said: \That Jihad is the best in which the mujahid's horse is killed and its blood is shed\"""
"2430","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) was asked: Which is the best deed? He said: \Believing in Allah and His Messenger.\"" It was asked: Which action is better after that? He said: \""Doing Jihad in the way of Allah.\"" It was asked: Then which action is better? He said: \""Hajj Mabarur.\"""""
"2431","Sayyidna Mu'adh bin Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \He who fights in the way of Allah until a camel milks twice"
"2432","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace be upon him) passed by those who were sitting. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Shall I not tell you the person who is the best in the sight of Allah?\"" He said: Surely"
"2433","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever stands in a row in the way of Allah"
"2434","It was narrated from Abdullah bin Sulaiman that Malik bin Abdullah passed by Habib bin Muslimah or Habib passed by Malik who was walking on foot holding his horse. He said: Why don't you get on board? May Allah guide you, said: Verily the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever has both his feet dusted in the way of Allah"
"2435","On the authority of Sayyiduna Sahl bin Saad, may Allah be pleased with him: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \A morning spent in the way of Allah or an evening spent in the way of Allah is better than anything in the world.\"""""
"2436","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever fasts one day in the way of Allah for the sake of Allah"
"2437","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Abu Rihanah that he was in a battle with the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he heard him saying: \Forbidden to Hell is the eye that wakes up in the way of Allah"
"2438","On the authority of Sayyidna Uqbah bin Amir Jahni (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) said: \May Allah have mercy on the guard of the army.\"" \n Imam al-Darmi"
"2439","Sayyiduna Abu Mas'ud Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) said: A companion came with a camel with a mahar (nickel) and said that it is (a gift) in the way of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \On the Day of Resurrection"
"2440","Sa'sa' bin Mu'awiya said: I met Sayyidna Abu Dharr who was carrying his camel and a musket was hanging around his neck. I said: O Abu Dharr! what is it what happened to you He said: This is my job. I then asked: What has happened to you? Then he replied: This is my job. I said: Narrate any such hadith that you have heard from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: \Whoever spends (gives) a couple of rupees in the way of Allah"
"2441","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aamir (may Allah be pleased with him) recited this noble verse (translation): \Prepare for the disbelievers as much force as you can. Listen: Force means: shooting arrows.\"""""
"2442","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aamir (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: “Allah the Exalted will admit three men to Paradise because of one arrow, the one who made the arrow if he had a good intention in making it, the one who helped him and the one who wielded the arrow.” Then the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: “Archery, ride, and to me archery is more beloved than riding.” To shoot, and to train a horse, and to play with one's wife, these three sports are right.\ And he said: \""Whoever abandons shooting after learning it has been ungrateful to the one who taught him.\"""""
"2443","Sayyidina Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Whoever is injured in the way of Allah"
"2444","Sahl bin Umama bin Sahl bin Hanif narrated a hadith from his grandfather through his father that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever asks for martyrdom with a sincere heart"
"2445","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \A martyr suffers as much from being killed as one of you suffers from an ant bite.\"""""
"2446","Sayyiduna Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, said that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \There is no soul who dies and enters Paradise"
"2447","Masrooq, may Allah have mercy on him, said that we asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, about the souls of the martyrs. And if it was not for Sayyiduna Abdullah (RA), he would not have told us any Hadith. He said: The souls of the martyrs will be in the sight of Allah on the Day of Resurrection in the form of green birds, which will live in lanterns hanging from the Throne, and will move about wherever they want in Paradise, and then return to their lanterns. Their Lord (Lord of the Worlds) will look at them and ask: \Do you need anything?\"" Those spirits will say: We do not need anything else except to return to the world and then be killed again (i.e. martyred)."""
"2448","Utbah bin Abdul Salmi said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \There are three types of those who are killed: (1) A believer who fought with his life and wealth in the way of Allah"
"2449","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and gave a sermon: Praise and worship of Allah, then he mentioned Jihad, and he did not leave anything that is better than Jihad (i.e. said Jihad to be the best) except duties. A Companion stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah! Tell me, if a person is killed in the way of Allah, will his mistakes be forgiven? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Yes"
"2450","It was narrated from Sayyidna Safwan bin Umayyah that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The plague (dying) is martyrdom"
"2451","Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Fighting in the way of Allah is martyrdom"
"2452","Sayyidna Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: We used to participate in the Ghazwat with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). At that time, we had nothing to eat except the leaves of the tree. We were treated like goats, that is, we were not mixed (treated like magnii). (Samar and Warak al-Hablah refer to the leaves of the tree)."
"2453","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Ubadah bin Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever does Jihad in the way of Allah and has no intention in his struggle but a rope"
"2454","Sayyidna Mu'adh bin Jabal (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \There are two kinds of Jihad"
"2455","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever does not fight jihad"
"2456","It was narrated from Sayyidna Zaid bin Khalid al-Jahni that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever gives equipment to a warrior in the way of Allah and guards the household of a Ghazi behind him in a benevolent way"
"2457","Sayyidna Bara bin Azib (RA) says that when this noble verse: “(﴿La Yastwi al-Qa’idun ........... Alkh)” was revealed, the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) called Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit (RA) and he came with a broad shoulder bone and wrote down this verse. (Verse: Surah Nisa: 95/4)."
"2458","Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) said: (His aunt) Sayyida Umm Haram bint Malhan (RA) narrated to me a hadith that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) said Qilaula one day in her house, and when he woke up, he was laughing. What made you laugh? He said: \I saw (in a dream) some people of my ummah riding on this sea (for Jihad) like kings riding on the throne.\"" I said: Pray for me too"
"2459","Sayyidah Umm Atiya (Nusiba bint Al-Harith) said: I participated in seven campaigns with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"2460","Sayyida Ayesha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go out, he used to draw lots for the names of his wives."
"2461","Abu Salih, a freed slave of Sayyidna Uthman (RA) said: I heard Ameerul Momineen Sayyidna Uthman (RA) saying on the pulpit: I hid from you a hadith that I heard from the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) so that you would not leave me. They were: \To guard one day in the way of Allah is better than a thousand years and than to guard houses.\"""""
"2462","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aamir (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: \The chain of deeds of every dead person ends except the one who guards the path of Allah"
"2463","Sayyiduna Urwa al-Barqi, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Goodness and blessings will be tied to the foreheads of horses until the Day of Resurrection"
"2464","The previous example is mentioned in this document as well. The translation of the tradition has been mentioned above."
"2465","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, a companion said: O Messenger of Allah! I want to buy a horse, so which horse should I buy? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \Buy a black horse with white on the nose and upper lip"
"2466","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to make dangerous horses race from Hafia to Sania, and he used to make harmless horses race from Sania to Masjid Bani Zariq. And Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) was also among those who participated in this horse race."
"2467","Abul Baid said: During the governorship of Hajjaj and Haqm bin Ayyub at Basra, there was a horse race. So we went to meet him, he was in his palace in Zawiya at that time, we asked him and said: O Abu Hamza! Did you people bet on horses during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? And he said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, also used to make bets. Sayyidina Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) replied: Yes, by Allah, the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) placed a bet on his horse, which was called Sabha, and it won over everyone, and he (may God's prayers and peace be upon him) was very happy about it and he liked it very much. \n Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: \Anhishah\"" means \""amazing\""."""
"2468","On the authority of Sayyidina Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \Fight Jihad against the polytheists with your lives"
"2469","Sayyiduna Mughira bin Shuba (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \A group of my ummah will always prevail over the people until the command of Allah comes (i.e. death or resurrection) and even then they will prevail.\"""""
"2470","Ameerul Momineen Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: \Some people of my Ummah will always stick to the truth.\"""""
"2471","Sayyidna Abu Dharr Ghafari (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \After me there will be a nation in my ummah who will recite the Qur'an and will not descend from their circles (i.e. they will be inactive)"
"2472","On the authority of Sayyiduna Sakhar al-Ghamdi, may Allah be pleased with him: The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \O Allah"
"2473","Sayyidna Ka'b bin Malik (RA) said: It would have been rare that when the Messenger of Allah (SAW) intended to travel, he would have left on a day other than Thursday."
"2474","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The best companions (travelling companions) in the sight of Allah are those who are good to their companions"
"2475","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The best companions are four"
"2476","Salman bin Buraidah narrated from his father, Sayyiduna Buraidah, may Allah be pleased with him: He said: When the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, appointed a commander of a platoon, he used to command him that he himself should fear Allah and treat the Muslims who are with him with fear of Allah. Do not betray, do not commit adultery, and do not beat the child."
"2477","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, \Do not desire to fight the enemy"
"2478","It was narrated from Sayyidna Sahib Rumi, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray during the campaign of Hunain: “Allahumma bik ahawil . . . ."
"2479","Sulaiman bin Burida narrated from his father, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, appointed someone as the leader of a platoon, he used to command him: \When you meet a polytheist enemy"
"2480","Al-Qamah said: I narrated this hadith to Muqatil bin Hayyan, so he said: This same hadith was narrated to me by Muslim bin Haysam from Sayyidna Numan bin Muqrin, may Allah be pleased with him, and he narrated the same from the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"2481","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) said that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) did not fight any nation before inviting it (to Islam). \n Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: Sufyan did not hear this hadith from Ibn Abi Najih. (That is, this tradition is disconnected)."
"2482","It was narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to attack (the enemy) at the time of the Fajr prayer and try to listen."
"2483","Sayyiduna Aws bin Abi Aws Thaqfi (RA) said: I attended the service of the Messenger of Allah (SAW) with a delegation of Banu Thaqif and I was in a corner of the dome in which there was no one except the Messenger of Allah (SAW). He was sleeping. Suddenly a companion came to him and whispered. He (peace be upon him) said: \Go and kill him.\"" He said: Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \""Does he not bear witness that there is no god but Allah?\"" Shuba said: I doubt whether he said about the martyrdom of Muhammad. He said: Yes (he bears witness to this)"
"2484","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \The blood of a Muslim who believes in the word la ilaha illa Allah (Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah) is not halal"
"2485","Khalid bin Samir said: Abdullah bin Rabah Ansari came to us. The Ansar knew them as jurisprudents, they said: Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to us a hadith that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an army of nobles, they marched and stayed as long as Allah willed, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the pulpit and gave the order, so it was announced: “Al-Salaat-e-Jami’ah” means the prayer is ready."
"2486","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Mas'ud Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \He who is consulted must be trustworthy.\"""""
"2487","Sayyidna Ka'b bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to fight somewhere, he used to do Turia (hiding it from others)."
"2488","Sayyidna Salama bin Aku'a said: I fought a man and killed him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me his property and on that day our code word with Sayyidna Khalid bin Al-Waleed was \Ummat\"" which means kill (kill)."""
"2489","Sayyidina Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Fahri (RA) said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) in the Battle of Hunain on a hot day and we camped under the shade of trees. After that he narrated the whole story and told me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) filled his fist with clay and the person who was very close to him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed me that he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw this clay at the enemies and said: \Woe to their faces\"""
"2490","Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit (RA) said: We were in a meeting with the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) and he (PBUH) said to us: \Pledge allegiance to me that you will not associate anyone with Allah"
"2491","Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (may God be pleased with him) said: We were one thousand four hundred men on the occasion of Hudaybiyyah. We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, and Sayyiduna Umar was holding his hand under the (shade) of a tree, it was a Samra (a wild tree that grows in the desert and is probably called the Kikar tree)."
"2492","Sayyiduna Bara bin Azib (may Allah be pleased with him) says: On the day of the Ahzab (trench) battle, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wash the mud with us, and because of the mud, the whiteness of his armpits was hidden, and he, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to hum these verses: \n (That is, \O Allah! If it were not for Your guidance"
"2493","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Anas that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah in the year of the conquest of Makkah, he placed himself on the blessed head of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Is this Ibn Khatl hanging from the curtains of the Kaaba? The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Kill him.\"""""
"2494","It was narrated on the authority of Anas that the handle of the Prophet's sword was made of silver. \n Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: Hisham al-Dastawi opposed it, he narrated it from Qatadah on the authority of Saeed bin Abi al-Hasan and he narrated it on the authority of the Prophet, peace be upon him, and the people understood that this is safe."
"2495","Sayyidina Abu Talha (RA) narrated that when the Prophet (PBUH) conquered a people, he liked to stay in their land for three days."
"2496","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) burned the gardens of Banunazir."
"2497","Sayyidina Abu Huraira al-Dawsi (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) sent us on a campaign and said: \If you succeed in capturing so-and-so"
"2498","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: In some of the battles of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, a woman was found who had been killed, so seeing this, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade the killing of women and children."
"2499","Sayyidna Aswad bin Saari, may Allah be pleased with him, said: We went on a campaign with the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and succeeded in arresting the idolaters. The people were quick to kill them and even started killing their children. When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard about this, he said: \What is the matter"
"2500","Atiya al-Qurazi said: (On the day when the people of Bani Qurayza were killed) we were brought before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and the one whose hair had grown was killed and the one whose hair had not grown was left, and I was among those whose hair had not grown."
"2501","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Musa (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) said: \Free the prisoner"
"2502","It was narrated from Sayyidina Imran bin Hussain (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) released one man in exchange for two men (i.e. released one unbeliever in exchange for two Muslim prisoners)."
"2503","(Marfu' Hadith) Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Mujahid, from 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr, from Abu Dharr: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""I was given five things not given to any prophet before me: I was sent to the red and the black (all mankind), the earth was made for me a mosque and a means of purification, spoils of war were made lawful for me and were not lawful for anyone before me, I was supported by awe (cast into the hearts of the enemy) for a month's journey—the enemy is frightened of me for a month's distance. And it was said to me: 'Ask, you shall be given.' I reserved my supplication for intercession for my Ummah, and it will reach, if Allah wills, whoever among you does not associate anything with Allah."""
"2504","Sayyiduna Abu Wail (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided the booty of Hunain into Jaarana. Imam al-Darmi (may God have mercy on him) said: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may God be pleased with him) is among his isnaads."
"2505","Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layli narrated from his father, he said: I was present with the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, at the time of the conquest of Khaybar. The polytheists were defeated. When we occupied their places of residence, the people rushed to the camels they found and immediately started boiling them in the pots, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered and all the pots were overturned. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided (the meat) between us and gave one goat to every ten people. Abu Laila said: There were only nine Banufals and I was alone. There was a goat for us too. \n Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: I have heard that Zayd bin Abi Anisa narrated this hadith from Qais bin Muslim, his purpose was that Zayd did not remember (this tradition is from the order) (but this is surprising on the part of Imam Darmi, may God have mercy on him, because Zayd may have heard it from the order and also from Qays bin Muslim)."
"2506","Zayd bin Abi Anisa on the authority of Qays bin Muslim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layli, on the authority of his father, and said: I turned to them (i.e. 9 persons). \n Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: The chain of transmission of Zakaria bin Adi is correct in my opinion."
"2507","Yazid bin Hurmuz said: Najda bin Amir wrote to Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) and inquired about some things, so Sayyidna Ibn Abbas (RA) wrote in reply, \Have you inquired about the share of relatives that Allah has mentioned (in the Qur'an)?\"" We believed that the relatives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) are the same relatives (i.e. we people)"
"2508","On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave three shares (of booty) to the horseman and one share to the footmen on the day of Khaibar."
"2509","In this manner, the above-mentioned hadith is narrated. The translation is above."
"2510","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I was present with the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) at the time of the distribution of booty, he (may God bless him and grant him peace) gave me a share except on the day of Khaibar, which was special only for the people of Hudaybiyah, and Sayyiduna Abu Musa and Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) came between Hudaybiyah and Khaybar."
"2511","The freed slave of Umayr Abul Laham said: I was a slave (of my master) when I came (to the battle) in Khyber, so the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave me a sword from among his personal possessions and said: \Hang it up.\"""""
"2512","It was narrated from Sayyidina Abu Umamah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling the shares before dividing them."
"2513","Hanash al-Sanaani narrated: We waged Jihad in the West and our Commander-in-Chief was Sayyidna Ruifa bin Thabit Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him). We conquered a village which used to be called Jarba, then Sayyidna Ruifa bin Thabit Ansari stood among us as a speaker and said: I stood among you because I heard from the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"2514","It was narrated from Sayyidna Abul Darda' (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) saw a pregnant woman lying at the door of the tent and said: \Perhaps her owner has intercourse with her?\"" The people said: Yes"
"2515","It was narrated from Abu Abd al-Rahman Habli that Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (RA) was in an army and children and their mothers were separated. When he saw the children, they were crying, so he returned each child to its mother and he used to say: Verily, the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \He who separates his mother from her children"
"2516","Sayyidna Sakhr bin Aila (and some called Ghaila) said: I arrested the maternal grandmother of Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba Radi Allahu Anhu and took her to the service of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace. Sayyidna Mughira, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, for his maternal grandmother. Hand it over to Mughira.” \n And Bani Salim had a spring of water. When he accepted Islam, he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and demanded its return. He (peace be upon him) called me and said: \O Rock! When people accept Islam"
"2517","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) sent a group in which Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) himself was also present."
"2518","Sayyidna Ubada bin Samit (RA) said that when the Prophet (PBUH) attacked the enemy's land, he would give a reward of one-fourth of the booty, and when all the people returned (and there was a need for war again), he would give a reward of one-third of the booty."
"2519","It was narrated from Sayyiduna Habib bin Muslimah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave an additional reward of one-third after Khums."
"2520","On the authority of Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever kills an unbeliever"
"2521","Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I fought with a disbelieving man and killed him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me his property."
"2522","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Ubadah bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked rewards and said: \A strong (powerful) Muslim should give away the booty to a weak Muslim.\"""""
"2523","It was narrated from Sayyidna Ubadah that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Pay even the needle and the thread and avoid betrayal"
"2524","Hanash Sanani said: We fought in the west with Sayyidna Ruifa bin Thabit Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, and we conquered a village called Jarba. At that time, Sayyidna Ruifa bin Thabit Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, stood among us to give a sermon, and said: I have stood among you at this time because I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, when he stood among us after Khaybar, he said: \Whoever worships Allah and the Day of Resurrection.\"" If he believes in the Hereafter"
"2525","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) said: Sayyidna Umar Ibn Al-Khattab (RA) narrated to me the hadith that how many companions were martyred on the day of Khaibar. People started saying: So-and-so is a martyr until they mentioned a man that he is a martyr. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Not at all"
"2526","Salim bin Abdullah narrated it from his father, from his grandfather Sayyiduna Umar. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \When you find someone who has stolen from the booty"
"2527","Kathir bin Abdullah bin Umar bin Awf Muzni narrated from his father, he narrated from his grandfather Sayyiduna Amr bin Awf, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \No robbery is permissible"
"2528","Junada bin Abi Umayyah said, \If I had not listened to Sayyidna Basr bin Arta'ah"
"2529","Sayyidna Abu Hameed Sa'idi (RA) reported that the Prophet (PBUH) entrusted a worker with the responsibility of receiving charity. It is for you (i.e. the money of Bait al-Mal) and it was gifted to me (is wealth). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Then why don't you stay in your father's and mother's house"
"2530","It was narrated from Anas bin Malik (RA) that the king of Dhi-Yazn sent a gift to the Prophet (PBUH) by buying one halah for 33 camels or 33 camels, which the Prophet (PBUH) accepted."
"2531","Sayyidina Abu Hameed Sa'idi (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The ruler of Elah sent a letter to the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) and sent a gift of a white mule."
"2532","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \We do not take help from polytheists.\"""""
"2533","From this chain of narrators, Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated it in the same context."
"2534","Sayyiduna Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah (RA) said: The last thing that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said was: \Eliminate the Jews from the Hijaz and the people of Najran from the Arabian Peninsula.\"""""
"2535","Sayyidna Abu Tha'laba Khoshni (RA) narrated: I came to the service of the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) and said: O Messenger of Allah! We live in the land of people of the book, so can we eat from their dishes? The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Even if you live in such a land as you have described"
"2536","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mughfil (RA) said: On the day of Khyber, a cup of fat was thrown, I came and grabbed it, and I said: I will not give anything from it to anyone today. Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: It is hoped that Hameed (bin Hilal) heard this from Sayyidna Abdullah bin Mughfil (may God be pleased with him)."
"2537","Bajla said: Sayyiduna Umar did not take jizya from the Magi until Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf testified that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, took jizya from the Magi of Hijr."
